course: dictionary
lesson: 4577
title: Helots: people without freedom
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A helot was a person in ancient Sparta, a city in Greece. Helots worked the land so that Spartan citizens could train as soldiers. «Sparta relied on a huge enslaved people, the helots, to farm for them.» Relied means depended on, so Sparta depended on the helots to grow its food.
explain: Helots were not free. They could not leave the land they worked, so they were almost like slaves. Read the clues in the sentence: enslaved and farm for them tell you they had to work for other people.
explain: The word helot has a second, rarer meaning. Today, a formal writer might call anyone treated like a slave or a serf a helot. A serf was a worker tied to a lord's land in medieval Europe, so the word is close in meaning to serf and slave.
fact: A helot was a person in ancient Sparta who worked the land.
fact: Helots could not leave the land they worked.
fact: «Helot» is a history word, and it is also used in a formal way for anyone treated like a slave or serf.
fact: Spartans feared helot rebellions, so they treated the helots harshly.
fact: Helot and serf are close in meaning, but a serf is a word from medieval Europe, not Sparta.
exercise: «Sparta relied on a huge enslaved people, the helots, to farm for them.» Who did the farming? | The Greek gods | *The helots | The Spartan soldiers | The sea merchants
exercise: Helots could not leave the land they worked. What does this tell you about them? | They were rich landowners | *They were not free to go where they wanted | They were children at school | They chose to stay because they loved the land
exercise: «Sparta relied on a huge enslaved people, the helots, to farm for them.» Find and copy one word that means forced to work without freedom. | *enslaved | huge | farm | Sparta
test: Which word means nearly the same as helot in its second meaning? | Farmer | Soldier | *Serf | Citizen
test: Why did the Spartans fear the helots? | *They might rise up against them | They had too many horses | They wanted to become helots | They were too lazy to farm
exam: In «Sparta relied on a huge enslaved people, the helots, to farm for them», what does relied mean? | paid for | forgot about | *depended on | fought against
